WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:05.230
We do have big news that I don't want to go
overly crazy about because of how it will

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:06.300
probably turn out.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.639
The big news is that Donald Trump's former
national security advisor, one of Trump's

00:00:10.639 --> 00:00:15.839
former national security advisors, John Bolton,
one of the architects of the Iraq war says

00:00:15.839 --> 00:00:19.970
he's willing to testify in the Senate impeachment
trial of Donald Trump.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:22.619
He says he would do it if he is subpoenaed.

00:00:22.619 --> 00:00:27.029
That's typical in these situations to say
you will show up if you are subpoenaed, uh,

00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:31.570
because you don't want to be accused of willingly
showing up to bad mouth someone, but it's

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:34.270
not totally clear that that's actually what
John Bolton would do.

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:36.000
We just don't know.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.980
Bolton said in a statement yesterday quote,
I have concluded that if the Senate issues

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.550
a subpoena for my testimony, I am prepared
to testify.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:51.020
Now, of course, whether he would be subpoenaed
by a Republican Senate is a real open question.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:55.070
Republicans are likely to run the trial as
Mitch McConnell has admitted in the way that's

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.840
most beneficial to Donald Trump after Bolton
and Trump's falling out.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:03.860
It's very difficult to imagine that a Bolton
testimony would actually be in Donald Trump's

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:04.860
interest.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:10.790
But nevertheless, Trump, uh, a Bolton rather
publicly saying this does put some pressure

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:13.490
on Republicans, uh, to bring them in.

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:18.260
Now, Marco Rubio, Republican Senator from
Florida came up with a completely cockamamie

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:21.760
excuse for why he doesn't think Bolton should
testify.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:27.280
It was something about, I'm paraphrasing here,
I think he said it's a Manu Rajo of CNN.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:34.000
It was something along the lines of, well,
the impeachment articles were based not on

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.170
John Bolton's testimony.

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:42.229
So I think that the impeachment trial in the
Senate should be based on the same things

00:01:42.229 --> 00:01:45.170
that the articles were voted on in the house.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:49.200
Sort of saying like, if Bolton wasn't part
of the proceedings in the house, he shouldn't

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.200
be called in the Senate.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.610
It was ridiculous.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.909
You know, a number of different legal analyses
say it makes no sense whatsoever.

00:01:54.909 --> 00:01:59.820
Now, as an update, uh, the president has been
impeached by the house of representatives,

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:00.820
speaker of the house.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:04.740
Nancy Pelosi has not yet sent the articles
of impeachment, both.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:08.799
There's two of them, uh, to the Senate, which
is required to get the trial going.

00:02:08.799 --> 00:02:13.900
Remember that John Bolton previously declined
to participate in the house's impeachment

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:18.219
investigation saying that he was directed
by the Trump administration not to comply

00:02:18.219 --> 00:02:19.310
with Congress.

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:25.469
He said, if you subpoena me, if federal courts
uphold the subpoena, I will testify the committees

00:02:25.469 --> 00:02:28.519
ultimately did not issue a subpoena for his
testimony.

00:02:28.519 --> 00:02:32.370
Now there is something interesting about the
subpoena of John Bolton.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:38.290
Many things in the Senate require a two thirds
majority to impeach a president and convict

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:39.290
them.

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:40.290
In the Senate.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:41.290
You need a two thirds majority.

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:46.420
You need two thirds of senators, meaning 67
of the a hundred senators to vote to convict.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:51.260
Right now there are 45 Democrats and two independents
who caucus with Democrats.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:53.870
That's 47 votes in the Senate.

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:59.239
You would need 20 Republican senators vote
to convict in order to remove Donald Trump,

00:02:59.239 --> 00:03:03.010
not likely to happen to subpoena John Bolton.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:06.140
You need only a simple majority meaning 51
senators.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:09.230
That means you need the 45 Democrats.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:13.519
The two independents who caucus with Democrats,
Bernie Sanders and Angus King, and then just

00:03:13.519 --> 00:03:18.319
for Republicans to sign on to subpoena John
Bolton.

00:03:18.319 --> 00:03:20.620
You actually could make this happen.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:24.620
If we go to our standard list of Republicans
who might do something logical.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:27.849
You've got Susan Collins from Maine, you've
got Lisa Murkowski from Alaska.

00:03:27.849 --> 00:03:30.349
You've gotten maybe Mitt Romney, uh, from
Utah.

00:03:30.349 --> 00:03:33.790
People talk about over about what, about Cory
Gardner from Colorado.

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:35.549
It's possible.

00:03:35.549 --> 00:03:41.699
The idea of Bolton being willing to testify
if subpoenaed is also funny.

00:03:41.699 --> 00:03:46.059
If you are subpoenaed, you were required by
law to show up.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:49.670
They're talking about it like it's a choice
and he would make the right choice.

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:55.719
Now that's an issue that maybe will come up
if, um, uh, Bolton is unwilling to respond

00:03:55.719 --> 00:04:01.249
to the subpoena, or if it is challenged by
the white house and it goes to federal courts,

00:04:01.249 --> 00:04:08.019
but Donald Trump clearly will do what he can
to prevent John Bolton from ultimately testifying.

00:04:08.019 --> 00:04:15.049
Imagine being Bolton who has loved the idea
of war with Iran for so long and now Trump

00:04:15.049 --> 00:04:19.540
waits until you're gone before trying to start
a war with Iran.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:22.140
He must just be furious and his neo-con boots.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:23.140
Don't you think?

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:28.169
Now as far as people getting super excited
about Bolton's testimony, even if he's subpoenaed

00:04:28.169 --> 00:04:32.729
and even if the subpoena is upheld by a federal
court and Bolton has to testify, he could

00:04:32.729 --> 00:04:35.360
choose to obfuscate unimportant issues.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.370
He could plead the fifth unimportant issues.

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:42.599
Bolton will do what is best for John Bolton
and that might be showing up in obfuscating.

00:04:42.599 --> 00:04:44.729
It might be showing up in self aggrandizing.

00:04:44.729 --> 00:04:46.550
It might be showing up and saying nothing.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:51.180
This guy is, not only is he no hero, he's
really one of the villains of American foreign

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:54.590
policy over the last 20 years and of course
of the Iraq war.

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:59.920
The only good thing here is that it puts a
little bit of pressure on Senate majority

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:04.349
leader Mitch McConnell to allow witnesses
because otherwise it would look like they

00:05:04.349 --> 00:05:07.979
are trying to silence Bolton, which they probably
are.

00:05:07.979 --> 00:05:13.280
But once again, if there's no consequences
for silencing John Bolton, why wouldn't they

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:14.280
do it?

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:51.949
It wouldn't

00:05:51.949 --> 00:06:50.949
make

00:06:50.949 --> 00:07:11.449
a difference.

